---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import PageHeader from '../components/PageHeader.astro';
import { PAGE_META } from '../data/pages';
import { pageSchema } from '../data/schema';
import { URLS } from '../data/site';
const meta = PAGE_META.privacy;
const breadcrumbs = [{label:'Home',href:'/'},{label:'Website privacy',href:meta.path}];
---
<BaseLayout title={meta.title} description={meta.description} structuredData={pageSchema(meta.path,meta.title,meta.description,breadcrumbs)}>
  <PageHeader eyebrow="website privacy" heading="What happens when you visit this site." lead="This page describes the website's hosting, analytics, and release lookups. Desktop application settings and provider credentials are a separate part of Git Workbench." breadcrumbs={breadcrumbs} />
  <article class="wrap document-body standalone-article">
    <section><h2>Website analytics</h2><p>The production website loads Google Analytics using measurement ID <code>G-0X03SJ62WK</code>. The Google tag measures website visits and interactions; depending on your browser and settings, it can use cookies and browser or device information. Development builds do not load the tag.</p><p>The website does not ask for access to local repositories, source files, Git credentials, or AI provider keys. Do not include private information in URLs or public GitHub issue reports.</p><p>See <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy">Google's privacy policy</a> and <a href="https://tools.google.com/dlpage/gaoptout">Google's Analytics opt-out browser add-on</a> for Google's data handling and an available browser control. Browser privacy settings and content blockers can also affect whether the tag loads.</p></section>
    <section><h2>Hosting and download requests</h2><p>This static website is hosted on GitHub Pages. GitHub handles the network requests required to serve it. See <a href="https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement">GitHub's privacy statement</a> for the hosting provider's practices.</p><p>The download section can request public release metadata from api.github.com to keep versions, file sizes, and installer links current. It sends no GitHub token from this website. Installers are downloaded from GitHub when you choose a download link.</p></section>
    <section><h2>The desktop application is separate</h2><p>Visiting this website does not configure the desktop application's hosting accounts or AI settings. Those connections are chosen inside the app. AI features send the requested change content to the provider you configure, including a local Ollama server when selected.</p><p>For application credential storage and setup behavior, read the <a href={URLS.firstRun}>first-run setup documentation</a> and <a href={URLS.branding}>application data locations</a>. For questions about the website, use the <a href="https://github.com/GitWorkbench/gitworkbench.github.io/issues">website issue tracker</a>.</p></section>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
